  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0026-p00026",
      "source_en": "In the New Year in the south, there was a day of heavy snow, and I went to Lingfeng to look for news of the spring plum. The fallen plum petals lay steeped in the snow, and I laughed and said, \"Its color is still short of three measures of brilliance.\" I said, \"By Destiny, you will hurry back to the capital before the Flower Festival, and I will prepare for you a truly vivid spring scene: white is still that cold, fluttering falling snow, but the plum blossoms are the hot blood of a thirteen-year-old boy.\" Written at the end of March, 1926.",
